# cdx-rl environment. Copy to config/env (gitignored) and adjust per box.
#
#   cp config/env.example config/env
#   set -a; . ./config/env; set +a
#
# Every path here points *outside* this repository. That is the shape of the
# thing: cdx-rl owns the method and the record, and borrows the engine and
# the trainer from a Cadex checkout it must not modify.

# The Cadex checkout. Read-only from cdx-rl's point of view: no commits, no
# edits, no branch changes. Wants go in cadex-wishlist.md.
CADEX_REPO=/home/theo/cadex

# The trainer's own virtualenv — plain venv, Python 3.12.3, mujoco 3.10.0,
# mujoco-mjx 3.10.0, jax 0.7.2 + cuda12. Separate from the engine's pixi
# environment on purpose (see cadex.md §"Two environments"). Never rebuild
# it: its pins are the reproducibility guarantee for every run recorded in
# the graph.
CADEX_TRAIN_VENV=/home/theo/cadex-train-venv

# Which engine to drive. Two routes, and on sb1x only one of them works.
#
# CADEX_ENGINE_DEV_TREE names a *built Cadex checkout*: its own FreeCADCmd
# (.pixi/envs/default/bin) plus its src/Mod/cadex. This is what cdx-rl uses,
# and the reason is not taste.
#
# CADEX_ENGINE_ROOT names a *staged payload* — the directory holding
# cadex-engine.json. It is the shipping shape and it is what `cadex --engine`
# was built for. The one staged on this box, at
# build/engine/cadex-engine-0.0.0-linux-x64, was assembled on 2026-07-31 and
# predates the entire MuJoCo surface. Measured, by asking it:
#
#   payload  assembly exports: assembly component connector joint solve
#                              motion simulation exploded_view
#   checkout assembly exports: ...those, plus dynamics mjcf task policy
#                              rollout body collision joint_dynamics actuator
#                              observation reward termination randomise
#                              reset_variation disturbance
#
# and its Mod/cadex has no CadexDynamics.py at all. Point cdx-rl at it and
# every script that declares a mechanism is refused with "assembly.mjcf is
# not defined", which reads like a script bug and is not one.
#
# The same trap applies to the CLI: `cadex` with CADEX_ENGINE_ROOT exported
# silently drives the stale payload, while `cadex` with it *unset* falls back
# to the development tree and works. So do not export CADEX_ENGINE_ROOT
# unless you mean the payload.
CADEX_ENGINE_DEV_TREE=/home/theo/cadex
# CADEX_ENGINE_ROOT=/home/theo/cadex/build/engine/cadex-engine-0.0.0-linux-x64

# Where training run directories land: one per dispatch, holding the model
# XML, the task bundle, progress.json, train.log and every .cxpolicy
# checkpoint. Gitignored; the graph carries what matters out of it.
CDXRL_JOBS=/home/theo/cdx-rl/jobs

# Where cdx-rl's own .cadex projects live. Gitignored — a project store is
# rebuildable from its script, and 2 MB per attempt is not history.
CDXRL_PROJECTS=/home/theo/cdx-rl/projects

# MUJOCO_GL is deliberately unset. The trainer is headless MJX and never
# opens a renderer, and nothing on this box has ever set it. If video
# rollout is ever added, set MUJOCO_GL=egl explicitly at that call site
# rather than exporting it here — an unexpected GL backend is a class of
# failure that only shows up on the box without a display.
